From 2eb7a2d75fd064542b5371ec7eeca6d341ba5b8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:31:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(gateway): route inference requests by namespace and
 endpoint protocol

The resolver reads the structured status.endpoints written by the
control plane, keeps only ready endpoints with a known protocol, and
forwards each request to the inference path of that protocol
(openai-chat: /v1/chat/completions, tgi-generate: /generate_stream)
instead of appending the inbound gateway path to the instance URL.

Requests to /api/v1/namespaces/{ns}/inference/{svc}/chat resolve the
service in that namespace; /api/v1/inference/{svc}/chat keeps resolving
services without a namespace. The cache key includes the namespace so
same-named services in different namespaces stay apart.
